# Minimum defensible publication portfolio

## Decision

Retain the existing **Paper B** and develop **two prospective mathematical papers**. Do not split the rotation algebra, contextuality classification, codebook theorem and teleportation separation into separate claims of independent discovery. Do not add a standalone bridge or folding article now. A broad laboratory/software paper is supplementary documentation until the primary results and software usability justify a later article.

This is a portfolio recommendation, not a claim that priority has already been established. The classification/resource manuscript has the stronger present center. The exact-query manuscript is coherent enough to draft, but its standalone publication status is particularly sensitive to a theorem-level search in modal/finite-semiring query literature.

## Existing Paper B: update, do not duplicate

**Question:** When does typed signed-frame operator fusion reduce total Boolean computation?

Its mathematical center is a correctly typed operator-level pipeline, not a claim to invent truth tables, matrix logic, NPN/cut manipulation or pointwise Boolean combination. Add the supplied S1/S2 mechanism evidence and matched generic-equality finding as exploratory results. Preserve the planned confirmatory evaluation boundary. There is no current evidential reason to spin folding out into another paper.

The best computational outcome need not be a unique simplification. If explicit CM metadata reaches the same folded form at lower total recognition, compile, reuse or memory cost, that is a valid useful result. If it does not, report the boundary without reverting to a weaker comparator. See [B_UPDATE_PLAN.md](B_UPDATE_PLAN.md).

## P01: Contextuality and Exact Information Resources over Finite Chain Rings

**Question:** Which valuation features govern possible-outcome nonlocality and exact communication tasks, and which distinctions survive a change of operations or tensor base?

**One-sentence contribution:** Under explicit complete-basis and fixed-orbit contracts, classify bipartite support models by Smith support and leading multiplicity, prove the d*h codebook formula, and separate this resource from universally faithful teleportation.

Use six primary clusters: residue-hyperplane criterion plus trichotomy (MOD-003/004); uniform Hardy construction (MOD-005); leading-layer codebooks and matched contextuality equivalence (RES-001/002); teleportation criterion and nilpotent/primitive separators (RES-003/004); tensor/enlarged-operation boundaries (MOD-001/009/010); binary two-setting obstruction (MOD-007). The last two expose the contract rather than inflate the headline count. Rotation and the enriched LM interface provide motivation and a compact bridge section; they are not the novelty claim.

The paper survives removal of all purported novelty in circulant algebra, base change, generic modal protocols and elementary rank facts. It does not survive unchanged if both the exact trichotomy and d*h theorem are already antecedented under the same contracts. In that event, retain any truly new operational comparison and rebuild as a focused synthesis/reproducibility article or note.

## P02: Exact Query Obstructions in Characteristic-Two Modal Computation

**Question:** What does exact all-outcomes-correct linear readout force in a pointwise Boolean-oracle model, despite the existence of nilpotent-ring phase kickback?

**One-sentence contribution:** Establish the exact Deutsch and BV bounds and the DJ one-query obstruction under the declared access contract, then distinguish genuine kickback from an invertible character readout.

Use four primary clusters: Deutsch (ALG-002), DJ (ALG-003), BV (ALG-004), and kickback/Fourier separation (ALG-005 with006/007). Exact discrimination (ALG-001) and the polynomial method are supporting antecedented ingredients. The known UNIQUE-SAT positive control (ALG-010) prevents an overbroad impossibility narrative. Do not headline finite Simon or failed conventional Grover circuits.

A dedicated targeted search has been performed, not a complete priority clearance. If the named query bounds are already present under the same assumptions, do not force a standalone article: a short comparative note requires a remaining substantive model separation; otherwise retain these results in the laboratory supplement. P02 imports only necessary algebra from P01, so it can be drafted without waiting for P01 acceptance.

## Why the tempting additional papers are rejected for now

**Standalone LM bridge:** most positive construction is scalar extension/naturality plus an explicit support predicate; the negative nonidentification and closure facts make it useful, but not a sufficiently strong independent article center. Place its concise statement in P01 and proofs in an appendix/supplement. Paper B's valuation theorem must only be cited.

**Standalone rotation/phase algebra:** the cyclic commutant, group-algebra quotient, nilpotence and parity/unit facts are standard or direct specializations. A coordinate convention alone is not a new algebra.

**Standalone folding performance:** S1/S2 demonstrate a mechanism and comparator equality, not a confirmatory natural-workload speed advantage. Keep in B unless a later campaign produces a distinctly stronger implementation story.

**Boolean Modal Laboratory:** use the consolidation and executable supplement now. A later software or pedagogy paper would need a stable API, installation/tutorial evidence, versioned corpus and a clear audience benefit, not another retelling of the same theorem bank.

## Order and overlap control

Draft P01 first. Draft P02 next after a concentrated exact-oracle prior-art pass; its proof review can proceed in parallel. Update B's evidence language now, but run its frozen performance campaign as a separate empirical workstream. Only then reassess whether a laboratory article adds value. [PAPER_OWNERSHIP_MATRIX.csv](PAPER_OWNERSHIP_MATRIX.csv) fixes one primary home for every claim, including supplementary and future-only records.

Primary home is not a novelty label: a known lemma can belong to the exposition of a paper without becoming its claimed discovery. Other manuscripts summarize or cite a primary theorem rather than resubmitting the same proof as new. Use stable canonical IDs during drafting, then retain an internal crosswalk to journal theorem numbers.
